From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:35:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Paint re-anchored abspos boxes at their DOM position

Taffy lays out every out-of-flow box against its CSS containing block,
and the paint tree lists such a box under that containing block, right
after the layout child it descends from. That still paints it above
later positioned boxes inside that child.

CSS 2.1 Appendix E paints a stacking context's z-index:auto positioned
boxes in tree order, so a positioned sibling that comes later in the DOM
must paint on top. todomvc is the everyday casualty: .filters is
abspos with left/right/bottom set and .footer is static, so .filters
anchors to .todoapp, paints over the whole footer and swallows every
click on the later .clear-completed button; "Clear completed" did
nothing on the react, preact, vue and angular builds alike.

layout/paint_tree.rs now lists (and hit-tests) a z-index:auto abspos
box whose containing block is not its flow parent under that flow
parent (paint_parent_override), with rehomed_paint_translate measured
from the box's oof_containing_block. Ordering within the merged list
uses document order explicitly rather than leaning on sort stability,
which no longer holds once re-homed boxes are appended. A z-indexed box
keeps its placement: its paint order is governed by z-index anyway.

taffy's bounds cannot cover a re-homed box (it is not a layout child of
its flow parent), and both hit-prune and paint-cull trust those bounds:
a select's overlay extends below the select, and abspos under a
zero-height <body> is outside it entirely, so hits and clipped
screenshots dropped them. compute_rehomed_reach runs after the
paint-tree build, which is where re-homes are recorded, unions each
host's re-homed boxes and propagates the rect up the layout-parent
chain; hit-prune and paint-cull widen their bounds by that reach. An
earlier flag-based variant simply disabled the shortcuts along flagged
chains; on heavy pages the flag reached the root, culling effectively
turned off, and the recorded scene ballooned until the renderer's wasm
aborted mid-screenshot.

rehomed_reach is rebuilt at resolve time, but pure-scroll frames skip
resolve, so it can be stale by the scroll delta. live_rehomed_reach
reads scroll offsets live, the way rehomed_paint_translate does, for
paint-time consumers (a filter effect layer's clip cut a re-homed abspos
box by exactly the scroller's scrollX).
